From 138d179db4593a5953c277f290afb49233fbb200 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:20:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): support native tool calls while streaming

OpenAI-compatible streaming requests now carry `tools`/`tool_choice` when
the provider can emit native tool calls, and the SSE parser reassembles
`delta.tool_calls` fragments per index into complete tool calls. Streaming
results expose them in `StreamChatResult.tool_calls`, so the agent loop
executes them exactly like the non-streaming path (history gets the
assistant tool_calls message plus the tool results) instead of rendering
the provider markup as plain text.

- providers/root.zig: `StreamChatResult.tool_calls`, a model-aware
  `supports_streaming_native_tools` vtable capability (default false), and
  `emitChatResponseAsStream` now hands tool calls to the caller so blocking
  fallbacks keep working.
- providers/sse.zig: `DeltaToolCall`, `ToolCallAccumulator`, and
  `extractDeltaToolCalls`; `parseSseLine` returns a struct so one chunk can
  carry content, tool-call fragments, and usage together.
- providers/compatible.zig: advertise streaming native tools when
  `native_tools` is on and streaming is not disabled.
- providers/reliable.zig and providers/router.zig: forward the capability
  to the provider that actually serves the request, so wrapping a capable
  provider in a failover chain or a router no longer hides it.
- agent/root.zig: keep native tools enabled on streaming turns for such
  providers and forward the accumulated tool calls into the turn loop.

Other providers keep the text tool protocol while streaming.
